# /ideas/ IS NOT SERVED WHILE AN ADSENSE REVIEW IS OPEN.
#
# THE SCHEMA IS NOW LIVE. supabase/92_ideas_board.sql has been run on the project, so the
# reason this rule was first written (a visitor got a heading and the sentence "The ideas
# board is not set up on this project yet.", which is the worst thing a reviewer can land
# on) no longer applies. The board would work today.
#
# The open review is the ONLY thing still holding it, and it is holding it on purpose: a
# page of user-submitted text that appears mid-review is a new surface the reviewer did not
# start on, and there is nothing on it yet for them to read. Nothing has to be fixed before
# it goes up. It goes up when the review closes.
#
# THIS RULE IS THE SECOND LOCK, not the first. Cloudflare's own docs are unreachable from
# the sandbox this was written in, so whether _redirects wins over a matching static asset
# could not be verified, and a guess is not good enough when being wrong means a rejection.
# The files being absent is what actually keeps the path empty; this catches the case where
# somebody restores them before the review closes.
#
# NOT robots.txt Disallow, which was the other idea and is worse: robots.txt is public, so a
# Disallow line advertises the path to exactly the reviewer it is meant to hide it from.
#
# TO TURN THE BOARD ON: restore the page, delete these two lines, and read the comment at
# the top of ideas/index.html about what has to be true before it can be indexed or carry
# ads. The schema step is already done.
#
#   git checkout claude/perfect-season-curve-banner-n4z2md -- ideas/
#
# TAKE IT FROM THE BRANCH, NOT FROM COMMIT 7479e737, which is where this line used to point.
# The page was rewritten after that commit (renamed to Community Ideas, developer text
# taken off, its own runthe.gg header instead of the arcade banner), so 7479e737 restores a
# working page that is the wrong one, and nothing would fail to tell you.
/ideas /404.html 404
/ideas/* /404.html 404
